<title>FRANCE: Saint-Louis H1 net profit falls.</title>
<headline>Saint-Louis H1 net profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable			     262  vs	    468</p>
<p>    Net, pre-exceptional			 284 vs	     507</p>
<p>    Net exceptional losses			17 vs     loss   73</p>
<p>    Operating					770  vs	   1,527</p>
<p>    Turnover				    18,271  vs	  17,615</p>
<p>Net profit before exceptionals by sectors:</p>
<p>    Sugar					    241 vs	     216</p>
<p>    Prepared meals				  39 vs		53</p>
<p>    Mushrooms				  loss 15 vs   profit   14</p>
<p>    Paper					     79 vs	     296</p>
<p>    Group expenses				  60 vs		72</p>
<p>NOTE: In a statement Saint-Louis linked the 44 percent fall in net profit before exceptional items to a decline in the results of its paper business.</p>
<p>The Arjo Wiggins Appleton paper unit was hurt by lower volumes linked to massive customer de-stocking, it said.</p>
<p>While the prepared meals and mushroom units also experienced difficulties, a good sugar campaign allowed the Generale Sucriere unit to increase its profit.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
